>

<p>Agencies use this service two ways: as white-label capacity to resell under their own brand, or as a second opinion on audits their own team already ran. The output is an SEO-specific audit — technical, on-page, content, and backlinks — not a full website review padded with security and accessibility checks your clients didn't ask for.</p>

<h2 id="what-agencies-get">What Agencies Get</h2>

<p>Every agency engagement includes a report with no AuditWeb branding, editable findings so you can adjust language for your client's voice, a call with your account lead (not the client) to walk through findings before delivery, and volume pricing that drops per-audit cost as your monthly volume increases.</p>

<p>Reports arrive as a branded PDF template you control. We never contact your clients directly. Nothing in the deliverable references AuditWeb.</p>

<h2 id="two-ways-to-work-with-us">Two Ways to Work With Us</h2>

<p><strong>Full white-label.</strong> You sell the audit under your own service name. We do the technical work — crawl, analysis, report writing — and deliver a document ready to forward. Most agencies use this for overflow during busy months or to offer audits without hiring an in-house SEO analyst.</p>

<p><strong>Second opinion.</strong> Your team already ran an audit and wants an independent check before it goes to the client. We review your findings against our own crawl and flag anything missed, overstated, or under-prioritised. This costs less than a full audit and catches errors before a client sees them.</p>

